`src/style.css` contains starter styles you can wire into your distribution if your consumers need packaged CSS. React and React DOM are peer dependencies. TSPack keeps `manifest.tsx` as the project contract; `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, and `vite.config.ts` are compatibility/tooling projections.

The generated `package.json` is marked `private` so npm publication is not accidental. Use TSPack pack flows and review your consumer-facing exports before publishing.
